course: dictionary
lesson: 1178
title: Brooding: thinking, gloomy and sitting on eggs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so use the words around it to find the right one. Ask what the sentence is about: a person's thoughts, a dark sky, or an animal's eggs.
explain: «Ben sat brooding over his lost dog all afternoon.» Brooding here means thinking for a long time about something that makes you sad or worried. A brooding mood shows in how someone sits and thinks.
explain: «Brooding clouds rolled in over the hills.» Here brooding means dark, gloomy or threatening. The clouds look like they are about to bring a storm. Then there is the bird meaning: «The hen was brooding on her eggs in the straw» means she was sitting on them to keep them warm until they hatch.
explain: «The gastric-brooding frog of Australia raised its babies in its stomach.» This frog kept its young safe inside its body, a little like a bird keeping its eggs safe. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Brooding is an adjective (a brooding look), a verb form of brood (brood, broods, brooded, brooding), and a noun (a brooding).
fact: «Brooding» can mean thinking for a long time about something that makes you sad, worried or angry.
fact: «Brooding» can mean looking dark, gloomy or threatening, like brooding clouds.
fact: «Brooding» can describe birds, such as a hen sitting on eggs to keep them warm until they hatch.
fact: Phrases to know: «brooding over» (thinking hard about a problem), «a brooding silence» (a heavy, gloomy quiet), and «brooding hen» (a hen sitting on her eggs).
exercise: «He sat brooding over the broken window all afternoon.» What does brooding mean here? | Cleaning up the mess quickly | *Thinking hard and sadly about something | Sleeping deeply | Laughing loudly at a joke
exercise: «The hen was brooding on her eggs in the straw.» What is she doing? | Hiding from the fox | *Sitting on the eggs to keep them warm until they hatch | Running across the field | Singing to the farmer
exercise: Find the word in «brooding clouds» that tells you the sky looks dark and threatening. | clouds | *brooding | sky | rain
test: «The gastric-brooding frog of Australia raised its babies in its stomach.» What does brooding mean in this sentence? | Dancing with its babies | *Keeping its young safe until they are ready | Sleeping in the mud | Shouting at the babies to be quiet
test: Ella says brooding always means sad. What is the best reply? | It means happy and bright | *No, it can also describe a dark sky or a bird sitting on eggs | Yes, it always means sad and nothing else | It is the name of a bird
exam: Which sentence uses brooding to mean dark and threatening? | The hen was brooding on her eggs. | *Brooding clouds rolled in over the hills. | Ben spent the day brooding over his lost dog. | The frogs were brooding in the pond.
